     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The current FDA-approved amlodipine (Norvasc) label sets the maximum adult dose at 10 mg once daily, not 50 mg. The label doesn't support 50 mg for hypertension, coronary artery disease, or any other indication. Please check the label again, because I think the figure may have been misread or mixed up with another drug or unit.\n\nOverdoses of amlodipine at or above this range can cause profound, prolonged hypotension and shock. They can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and the effects can last more than 24 hours because of the drug's long half-life.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **5 mg PO once daily**\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the label maximum\n- **2.5 mg PO once daily**\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason to go beyond the label, such as a documented plan from cardiology or pharmacy, I'd suggest getting that reviewed and documented first. I can then enter the order with the note, but I'm not comfortable submitting it on the basis of the label claim."
      }
